From 56c16d9c89a8c415ac84e56ae926d788391a5c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:35:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 41/51] Fix the invisible dictionary senses and refine the word
 popup

The dictionary senses were rendered but invisible: the content rows
resolved their text colors in code against the activity theme, while
the popup itself renders with the dialog's own light theme - a dark
activity theme produced light text on the light dialog, so the
phonetic and exam labels (theme attributes in the layout) showed
while every sense row stayed blank. The rows now reuse the colors the
theme already renders on the fixed popup views, so they are exactly
as readable as the headline.

The player's popup becomes a compact dark translucent overlay instead
of an opaque light dialog that covers the video: rounded near-black
background the video faintly shines through, light text, capped
width. The reader keeps the light variant. Both variants are a notch
smaller overall.

With the new pause-on-lookup setting on (default), tapping a word in
the player pauses playback while the popup is open and resumes it
when it closes, so the video does not run past the sentence the
learner is reading about.

The dictionary source itself is now selectable in the settings: the
Youdao dictionary (default) or the free Microsoft translator endpoint
the subtitle translation already uses - a plain translation without
phonetics or senses, as a fallback for users Youdao does not work
for. (dictionaryapi.dev was evaluated and dropped: Cloudflare
challenges make it unusable from a plain HTTP client.)
